IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc18-weapons-evidence.l4 -- the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 491 to 492 (forfeiture of weapons and ammunition, restitution or forfeiture of
-- property obtained by crime, photographic evidence, seizure of explosives). Part agent ccc18; layer 1. The section 2 and 2.1 terms (weapon, firearm, explosive substance, ...)
-- are taken from the keel as MAYBE BOOLEAN inputs (PLAN.md section 4); offences named by section number are tested against the core's `Provision of the Code` (rule R1).
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN (or MAYBE / total types where the text closes the list); see the header of `ccc18-soira-notice`, `ccc18-forfeiture` and NOTES.md.

§ `Sections 491 to 492 -- Forfeiture of weapons, restitution, photographic evidence, explosives`

§ `491 Forfeiture of weapons and ammunition`

-- src:10851 | Forfeiture of weapons and ammunition
-- src:10852 | 491 (1) Subject to subsection (2), where it is determined by a court that
-- src:10853 | (a) a weapon, an imitation firearm, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance was used in the commission of an offence and that thing has been seized and detained, or
-- src:10854 | (b) that a person has committed an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, a firearm, a cross-bow, a prohibited weapon, a restricted weapon, a prohibited device, a firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance and any such thing has been seized and detained,
-- src:10855 | the thing so seized and detained is forfeited to Her Majesty and shall be disposed of as the Attorney General directs.
@ref Criminal Code s 491(1) (src:10851-10855)
DECLARE `s 491(1) the thing` HAS
    `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2.1 imitation firearm: the thing is a imitation firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2.1 prohibited device: the thing is a prohibited device` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2.1 firearm part: the thing is a firearm part` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2.1 ammunition: the thing is a ammunition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2.1 prohibited ammunition: the thing is a prohibited ammunition` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is a explosive substance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2.1 cross-bow: the thing is a cross-bow` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2.1 prohibited weapon: the thing is a prohibited weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `s 2.1 restricted weapon: the thing is a restricted weapon` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

@ref Criminal Code s 491(1) (src:10851-10855)
GIVEN `it is determined by a court that the thing was used in the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is determined by a court that the person has committed an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, the thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing has been seized and detained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing` IS A `s 491(1) the thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491(1) the thing is forfeited to Her Majesty` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the thing has been seized and detained` AND (`it is determined by a court that the thing was used in the commission of an offence` OR `it is determined by a court that the person has committed an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, the thing`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where it is determined by a court that (a) a weapon, an imitation firearm, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance was used in the commission of an offence and that thing has been seized and detained" [marginal (a)]
    ELSE IF (`it is determined by a court that the thing was used in the commission of an offence` AND (`the thing`'s `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 imitation firearm: the thing is a imitation firearm` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 prohibited device: the thing is a prohibited device` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 firearm part: the thing is a firearm part` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 ammunition: the thing is a ammunition` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 prohibited ammunition: the thing is a prohibited ammunition` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is a explosive substance` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) OR (`it is determined by a court that the person has committed an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, the thing` AND (`the thing`'s `s 2.1 prohibited device: the thing is a prohibited device` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 firearm part: the thing is a firearm part` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 ammunition: the thing is a ammunition` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 prohibited ammunition: the thing is a prohibited ammunition` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is a explosive substance` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 cross-bow: the thing is a cross-bow` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 prohibited weapon: the thing is a prohibited weapon` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 restricted weapon: the thing is a restricted weapon` EQUALS JUST TRUE))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF (`it is determined by a court that the thing was used in the commission of an offence` AND (`the thing`'s `s 2 weapon: the thing is a weapon` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 imitation firearm: the thing is a imitation firearm` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 prohibited device: the thing is a prohibited device` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 firearm part: the thing is a firearm part` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 ammunition: the thing is a ammunition` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 prohibited ammunition: the thing is a prohibited ammunition` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is a explosive substance` EQUALS NOTHING)) OR (`it is determined by a court that the person has committed an offence that involves, or the subject-matter of which is, the thing` AND (`the thing`'s `s 2.1 prohibited device: the thing is a prohibited device` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 firearm part: the thing is a firearm part` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 ammunition: the thing is a ammunition` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 prohibited ammunition: the thing is a prohibited ammunition` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is a explosive substance` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2 firearm: the thing is a firearm` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 cross-bow: the thing is a cross-bow` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 prohibited weapon: the thing is a prohibited weapon` EQUALS NOTHING OR `the thing`'s `s 2.1 restricted weapon: the thing is a restricted weapon` EQUALS NOTHING))
              THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the kinds of thing are defined in sections 2 and 2.1, answered by the keel
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a weapon, an imitation firearm, a prohibited device, a firearm part, any ammunition, any prohibited ammunition or an explosive substance was used in the commission of an offence" [marginal (a)]

-- src:10856 | Return to lawful owner
-- src:10857 | (2) If the court by which a determination referred to in subsection (1) is made is satisfied that the lawful owner of any thing that is or may be forfeited to Her Majesty under subsection (1) was not a party to the offence and had no reasonable grounds to believe that the thing would or might be used in the commission of an offence, the court shall order that the thing be returned to that lawful owner, that the proceeds of any sale of the thing be paid to that lawful owner or, if the thing was destroyed, that an amount equal to the value of the thing be paid to the owner.
@ref Criminal Code s 491(2) (src:10856-10857)
DECLARE `s 491(2) state of the thing` IS ONE OF
    `s 491(2) the thing is still held`
    `s 491(2) the thing was sold`
    `s 491(2) the thing was destroyed`

@ref Criminal Code s 491(2) (src:10856-10857)
DECLARE `s 491(2) order` IS ONE OF
    `s 491(2) the thing is returned to the lawful owner`
    `s 491(2) the proceeds of the sale of the thing are paid to the lawful owner`
    `s 491(2) an amount equal to the value of the thing is paid to the owner`
    `s 491(2) no order for return or payment is required by this subsection`

@ref Criminal Code s 491(2) (src:10856-10857)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied that the lawful owner of the thing was not a party to the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the lawful owner had no reasonable grounds to believe that the thing would or might be used in the commission of an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      state IS A `s 491(2) state of the thing`
GIVETH A `s 491(2) order`
`s 491(2) the order the court shall make` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied that the lawful owner of the thing was not a party to the offence` AND `the court is satisfied that the lawful owner had no reasonable grounds to believe that the thing would or might be used in the commission of an offence`
    THEN CONSIDER state
         WHEN `s 491(2) the thing is still held` THEN `s 491(2) the thing is returned to the lawful owner`
         WHEN `s 491(2) the thing was sold` THEN `s 491(2) the proceeds of the sale of the thing are paid to the lawful owner`
         WHEN `s 491(2) the thing was destroyed` THEN `s 491(2) an amount equal to the value of the thing is paid to the owner`
    ELSE `s 491(2) no order for return or payment is required by this subsection`   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "was not a party to the offence and had no reasonable grounds to believe that the thing would or might be used in the commission of an offence" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 491(2) (src:10856-10857)
DECLARE `s 491(2) action` IS ONE OF `s 491(2) order that the thing be returned to the lawful owner, that the proceeds of any sale of the thing be paid to that lawful owner or, if the thing was destroyed, that an amount equal to the value of the thing be paid to the owner`

@ref Criminal Code s 491(2) (src:10856-10857)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 491(2) action`
`s 491(2) the duty of the court to order the return or payment` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 491(2) order that the thing be returned to the lawful owner, that the proceeds of any sale of the thing be paid to that lawful owner or, if the thing was destroyed, that an amount equal to the value of the thing be paid to the owner`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court was satisfied of the owner's innocence and made no order for return or payment"

-- src:10858 | Application of proceeds
-- src:10859 | (3) Where any thing in respect of which this section applies is sold, the proceeds of the sale shall be paid to the Attorney General or, where an order is made under subsection (2), to the person who was, immediately prior to the sale, the lawful owner of the thing.
@ref Criminal Code s 491(3) (src:10858-10859)
DECLARE `s 491(3) recipient of the proceeds` IS ONE OF
    `s 491(3) the Attorney General`
    `s 491(3) the person who was, immediately prior to the sale, the lawful owner of the thing`

@ref Criminal Code s 491(3) (src:10858-10859)
GIVEN `the thing is sold` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 491(3) recipient of the proceeds`
`s 491(3) the person to whom the proceeds of the sale shall be paid` MEANS
    IF NOT `the thing is sold`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where any thing in respect of which this section applies is sold, the proceeds of the sale shall be paid"
    ELSE IF `an order is made under subsection (2)`
         THEN JUST `s 491(3) the person who was, immediately prior to the sale, the lawful owner of the thing`
         ELSE JUST `s 491(3) the Attorney General`

§ `491.1 Order for restitution or forfeiture of property obtained by crime`

-- src:10860 | Order for restitution or forfeiture of property obtained by crime
-- src:10861 | 491.1 (1) Where an accused or defendant is tried for an offence and the court determines that an offence has been committed, whether or not the accused has been convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence, and at the time of the trial any property obtained by the commission of the offence
-- src:10862 | (a) is before the court or has been detained so that it can be immediately dealt with, and
-- src:10863 | (b) will not be required as evidence in any other proceedings,
-- src:10864 | section 490 does not apply in respect of the property and the court shall make an order under subsection (2) in respect of the property.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.1(1) (src:10860-10864)
DECLARE `s 491.1(1) action` IS ONE OF `s 491.1(1) make an order under subsection (2) in respect of the property`

@ref Criminal Code s 491.1(1) (src:10860-10864)
GIVEN `the accused or defendant is tried for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court determines that an offence has been committed, whether or not the accused has been convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property was obtained by the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) at the time of the trial the property is before the court or has been detained so that it can be immediately dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) at the time of the trial the property will not be required as evidence in any other proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.1(1) the court shall make an order under subsection (2) in respect of the property` MEANS
    IF `the accused or defendant is tried for an offence` AND `the court determines that an offence has been committed, whether or not the accused has been convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence` AND `the property was obtained by the commission of the offence` AND `(a) at the time of the trial the property is before the court or has been detained so that it can be immediately dealt with` AND `(b) at the time of the trial the property will not be required as evidence in any other proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an accused or defendant is tried for an offence and the court determines that an offence has been committed" [marginal (a)]

@ref Criminal Code s 491.1(1) (src:10860-10864)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 491.1(1) action`
`s 491.1(1) the duty of the court to make an order in respect of the property` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 491.1(1) make an order under subsection (2) in respect of the property`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the circumstances of subsection (1) existed and the court made no order under subsection (2)"

-- src:10860 | Order for restitution or forfeiture of property obtained by crime
-- src:10861 | 491.1 (1) Where an accused or defendant is tried for an offence and the court determines that an offence has been committed, whether or not the accused has been convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence, and at the time of the trial any property obtained by the commission of the offence
-- src:10862 | (a) is before the court or has been detained so that it can be immediately dealt with, and
-- src:10863 | (b) will not be required as evidence in any other proceedings,
-- src:10864 | section 490 does not apply in respect of the property and the court shall make an order under subsection (2) in respect of the property.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.1(1) (src:10860-10864)
GIVEN `the accused or defendant is tried for an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court determines that an offence has been committed, whether or not the accused has been convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property was obtained by the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) at the time of the trial the property is before the court or has been detained so that it can be immediately dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) at the time of the trial the property will not be required as evidence in any other proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.1(1) (section 490) section 490 does not apply in respect of the property` MEANS
    IF `the accused or defendant is tried for an offence` AND `the court determines that an offence has been committed, whether or not the accused has been convicted or discharged under section 730 of the offence` AND `the property was obtained by the commission of the offence` AND `(a) at the time of the trial the property is before the court or has been detained so that it can be immediately dealt with` AND `(b) at the time of the trial the property will not be required as evidence in any other proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "section 490 does not apply in respect of the property"

-- src:10865 | Idem
-- src:10866 | (2) In the circumstances referred to in subsection (1), the court shall order, in respect of any property,
-- src:10867 | (a) if the lawful owner or person lawfully entitled to possession of the property is known, that it be returned to that person; and
-- src:10868 | (b) if the lawful owner or person lawfully entitled to possession of the property is not known, that it be forfeited to Her Majesty, to be disposed of as the Attorney General directs or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.1(2) (src:10865-10868)
DECLARE `s 491.1(2) order` IS ONE OF
    `s 491.1(2)(a) the property is returned to the lawful owner or person lawfully entitled to possession`
    `s 491.1(2)(b) the property is forfeited to Her Majesty, to be disposed of as the Attorney General directs or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law`

@ref Criminal Code s 491.1(2) (src:10865-10868)
GIVEN `the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lawful owner or person lawfully entitled to possession of the property is known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 491.1(2) order`
`s 491.1(2) the order the court shall make` MEANS
    IF NOT `the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the circumstances referred to in subsection (1), the court shall order"
    ELSE IF `the lawful owner or person lawfully entitled to possession of the property is known`
         THEN JUST `s 491.1(2)(a) the property is returned to the lawful owner or person lawfully entitled to possession`
         ELSE JUST `s 491.1(2)(b) the property is forfeited to Her Majesty, to be disposed of as the Attorney General directs or otherwise dealt with in accordance with the law`

-- src:10869 | When certain orders not to be made
-- src:10870 | (3) An order shall not be made under subsection (2)
-- src:10871 | (a) in the case of proceedings against a trustee, banker, merchant, attorney, factor, broker or other agent entrusted with the possession of goods or documents of title to goods, for an offence under section 330, 331, 332 or 336; or
-- src:10872 | (b) in respect of
-- src:10873 | (i) property to which a person acting in good faith and without notice has acquired lawful title for valuable consideration,
-- src:10874 | (ii) a valuable security that has been paid or discharged in good faith by a person who was liable to pay or discharge it,
-- src:10875 | (iii) a negotiable instrument that has, in good faith, been taken or received by transfer or delivery for valuable consideration by a person who had no notice and no reasonable cause to suspect that an offence had been committed, or
-- src:10876 | (iv) property in respect of which there is a dispute as to ownership or right of possession by claimants other than the accused or defendant.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.1(3) (src:10869-10876)
GIVEN `(a) the proceedings are against a trustee, banker, merchant, attorney, factor, broker or other agent entrusted with the possession of goods or documents of title to goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(a) the proceedings are for an offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `(b)(i) the property is property to which a person acting in good faith and without notice has acquired lawful title for valuable consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b)(ii) the property is a valuable security that has been paid or discharged in good faith by a person who was liable to pay or discharge it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b)(iii) the property is a negotiable instrument that has, in good faith, been taken or received by transfer or delivery for valuable consideration by a person who had no notice and no reasonable cause to suspect that an offence had been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b)(iv) the property is property in respect of which there is a dispute as to ownership or right of possession by claimants other than the accused or defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.1(3) an order shall not be made under subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF (`(a) the proceedings are against a trustee, banker, merchant, attorney, factor, broker or other agent entrusted with the possession of goods or documents of title to goods`
        AND (  `(a) the proceedings are for an offence`'s `section` EQUALS 330 OR `(a) the proceedings are for an offence`'s `section` EQUALS 331
            OR `(a) the proceedings are for an offence`'s `section` EQUALS 332 OR `(a) the proceedings are for an offence`'s `section` EQUALS 336))
       OR `(b)(i) the property is property to which a person acting in good faith and without notice has acquired lawful title for valuable consideration`
       OR `(b)(ii) the property is a valuable security that has been paid or discharged in good faith by a person who was liable to pay or discharge it`
       OR `(b)(iii) the property is a negotiable instrument that has, in good faith, been taken or received by transfer or delivery for valuable consideration by a person who had no notice and no reasonable cause to suspect that an offence had been committed`
       OR `(b)(iv) the property is property in respect of which there is a dispute as to ownership or right of possession by claimants other than the accused or defendant`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order shall not be made under subsection (2) (a) in the case of proceedings against a trustee, banker, merchant, attorney, factor, broker or other agent entrusted with the possession of goods or documents of title to goods, for an offence under section 330, 331, 332 or 336"

-- src:10877 | By whom order executed
-- src:10878 | (4) An order made under this section shall, on the direction of the court, be executed by the peace officers by whom the process of the court is ordinarily executed.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.1(4) (src:10877-10878)
DECLARE `s 491.1(4) action` IS ONE OF `s 491.1(4) execute the order made under this section`

@ref Criminal Code s 491.1(4) (src:10877-10878)
GIVEN `the court directs that an order made under this section be executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.1(4) the peace officers shall execute the order` MEANS
    IF `the court directs that an order made under this section be executed` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is laid only where "on the direction of the court"

@ref Criminal Code s 491.1(4) (src:10877-10878)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `s 491.1(4) action`
`s 491.1(4) the duty of a peace officer` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `s 491.1(4) execute the order made under this section`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a peace officer` BECAUSE "the court directed that the order be executed and the peace officers did not execute it"

§ `491.2 Photographic evidence`

-- src:10879 | Photographic evidence
-- src:10880 | 491.2 (1) Before any property that would otherwise be required to be produced for the purposes of a preliminary inquiry, trial or other proceeding in respect of an offence under section 334, 344, 348, 354, 355.2, 355.4, 362 or 380 is returned or ordered to be returned, forfeited or otherwise dealt with under section 489.1 or 490 or is otherwise returned, a peace officer or any person under the direction of a peace officer may take and retain a photograph of the property.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.2(1) (src:10879-10880)
GIVEN `the proceeding is in respect of an offence` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the property would otherwise be required to be produced for the purposes of a preliminary inquiry, trial or other proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property has not yet been returned or ordered to be returned, forfeited or otherwise dealt with under section 489.1 or 490, or otherwise returned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a peace officer or a person under the direction of a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.2(1) the person may take and retain a photograph of the property` MEANS
    IF (  `the proceeding is in respect of an offence`'s `section` EQUALS 334 OR `the proceeding is in respect of an offence`'s `section` EQUALS 344
       OR `the proceeding is in respect of an offence`'s `section` EQUALS 348 OR `the proceeding is in respect of an offence`'s `section` EQUALS 354
       OR `the proceeding is in respect of an offence`'s `section` EQUALS 355.2 OR `the proceeding is in respect of an offence`'s `section` EQUALS 355.4
       OR `the proceeding is in respect of an offence`'s `section` EQUALS 362 OR `the proceeding is in respect of an offence`'s `section` EQUALS 380)
       AND `the property would otherwise be required to be produced for the purposes of a preliminary inquiry, trial or other proceeding`
       AND `the property has not yet been returned or ordered to be returned, forfeited or otherwise dealt with under section 489.1 or 490, or otherwise returned`
       AND `the person is a peace officer or a person under the direction of a peace officer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Before any property that would otherwise be required to be produced for the purposes of a preliminary inquiry, trial or other proceeding in respect of an offence under section 334, 344, 348, 354, 355.2, 355.4, 362 or 380 is returned or ordered to be returned, forfeited or otherwise dealt with under section 489.1 or 490 or is otherwise returned, a peace officer or any person under the direction of a peace officer may take and retain a photograph of the property"

-- src:10881 | Certified photograph admissible in evidence
-- src:10882 | (2) Every photograph of property taken under subsection (1), accompanied by a certificate of a person containing the statements referred to in subsection (3), shall be admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, shall have the same probative force as the property would have had if it had been proved in the ordinary way.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.2(2) (src:10881-10882)
GIVEN `the photograph was taken under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the photograph is accompanied by a certificate of a person containing the statements referred to in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.2(2) the photograph is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    IF `the photograph was taken under subsection (1)` AND `the photograph is accompanied by a certificate of a person containing the statements referred to in subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every photograph of property taken under subsection (1), accompanied by a certificate of a person containing the statements referred to in subsection (3), shall be admissible in evidence"

-- src:10881 | Certified photograph admissible in evidence
-- src:10882 | (2) Every photograph of property taken under subsection (1), accompanied by a certificate of a person containing the statements referred to in subsection (3), shall be admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, shall have the same probative force as the property would have had if it had been proved in the ordinary way.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.2(2) (src:10881-10882)
GIVEN `the photograph is admissible in evidence under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.2(2) the photograph has the same probative force as the property would have had if it had been proved in the ordinary way` MEANS
    IF NOT `the photograph is admissible in evidence under subsection (2)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision is about "Every photograph of property taken under subsection (1), accompanied by a certificate"
    ELSE IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary, shall have the same probative force as the property would have had if it had been proved in the ordinary way"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10883 | Statements made in certificate
-- src:10884 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2), a certificate of a person stating that
-- src:10885 | (a) the person took the photograph under the authority of subsection (1),
-- src:10886 | (b) the person is a peace officer or took the photograph under the direction of a peace officer, and
-- src:10887 | (c) the photograph is a true photograph
-- src:10888 | shall be admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is evidence of the statements contained in the certificate without proof of the signature of the person appearing to have signed the certificate.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.2(3) (src:10883-10888)
GIVEN `(a) the certificate of a person states that the person took the photograph under the authority of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(b) it states that the person is a peace officer or took the photograph under the direction of a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `(c) it states that the photograph is a true photograph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.2(3) the certificate is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    IF `(a) the certificate of a person states that the person took the photograph under the authority of subsection (1)` AND `(b) it states that the person is a peace officer or took the photograph under the direction of a peace officer` AND `(c) it states that the photograph is a true photograph`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate of a person stating that (a) the person took the photograph under the authority of subsection (1)"

-- src:10883 | Statements made in certificate
