      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.2(3) the certificate is evidence of the statements contained in it without proof of the signature of the person appearing to have signed it` MEANS
    IF NOT `the certificate is admissible in evidence under subsection (3)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the provision is about a certificate stating (a), (b) and (c)
    ELSE IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is evidence of the statements contained in the certificate without proof of the signature"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:10889 | Secondary evidence of peace officer
-- src:10890 | (4) An affidavit or solemn declaration of a peace officer or other person stating that the person has seized property and detained it or caused it to be detained from the time that person took possession of the property until a photograph of the property was taken under subsection (1) and that the property was not altered in any manner before the photograph was taken shall be admissible in evidence and, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, is evidence of the statements contained in the affidavit or solemn declaration without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the affidavit or solemn declaration.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.2(4) (src:10889-10890)
GIVEN `it is an affidavit or solemn declaration of a peace officer or other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the person has seized property and detained it or caused it to be detained from the time that person took possession of the property until a photograph of the property was taken under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that the property was not altered in any manner before the photograph was taken` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.2(4) the affidavit or solemn declaration is admissible in evidence` MEANS
    IF `it is an affidavit or solemn declaration of a peace officer or other person` AND `it states that the person has seized property and detained it or caused it to be detained from the time that person took possession of the property until a photograph of the property was taken under subsection (1)` AND `it states that the property was not altered in any manner before the photograph was taken`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An affidavit or solemn declaration of a peace officer or other person stating that the person has seized property and detained it"

