-- src:10891 | Notice of intention to produce certified photograph
-- src:10892 | (5) Unless the court orders otherwise, no photograph, certificate, affidavit or solemn declaration shall be received in evidence at a trial or other proceeding pursuant to subsection (2), (3) or (4) unless the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused a copy thereof and reasonable notice of intention to produce it in evidence.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.2(5) (src:10891-10892)
GIVEN `the court orders otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused a copy of the photograph, certificate, affidavit or solemn declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused reasonable notice of intention to produce it in evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.2(5) the photograph, certificate, affidavit or solemn declaration shall not be received in evidence` MEANS
    IF `the court orders otherwise`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless the court orders otherwise, no photograph, certificate, affidavit or solemn declaration shall be received in evidence"
    ELSE IF `the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused a copy of the photograph, certificate, affidavit or solemn declaration` AND `the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused reasonable notice of intention to produce it in evidence`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the prosecutor has, before the trial or other proceeding, given to the accused a copy thereof and reasonable notice of intention to produce it in evidence"
         ELSE JUST TRUE   -- the bar applies

-- src:10893 | Attendance for examination
-- src:10894 | (6) Notwithstanding subsection (3) or (4), the court may require the person who appears to have signed a certificate, an affidavit or a solemn declaration referred to in that subsection to appear before it for examination or cross-examination in respect of the issue of proof of any of the facts contained in the certificate, affidavit or solemn declaration.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.2(6) (src:10893-10894)
GIVEN `the person appears to have signed a certificate, an affidavit or a solemn declaration referred to in subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the examination or cross-examination is in respect of the issue of proof of any of the facts contained in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.2(6) the court may require the person who appears to have signed to appear for examination or cross-examination` MEANS
    IF `the person appears to have signed a certificate, an affidavit or a solemn declaration referred to in subsection (3) or (4)` AND `the examination or cross-examination is in respect of the issue of proof of any of the facts contained in it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may require the person who appears to have signed a certificate, an affidavit or a solemn declaration referred to in that subsection to appear before it for examination or cross-examination"

-- src:10895 | Production of property in court
-- src:10896 | (7) A court may order any property seized and returned pursuant to section 489.1 or 490 to be produced in court or made available for examination by all parties to a proceeding at a reasonable time and place, notwithstanding that a photograph of the property has been received in evidence pursuant to subsection (2), where the court is satisfied that the interests of justice so require and that it is possible and practicable to do so in the circumstances.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.2(7) (src:10895-10896)
GIVEN `the property was seized and returned pursuant to section 489.1 or 490` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that the interests of justice so require` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that it is possible and practicable to do so in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.2(7) the court may order the property to be produced in court or made available for examination` MEANS
    IF `the property was seized and returned pursuant to section 489.1 or 490` AND `the court is satisfied that the interests of justice so require` AND `the court is satisfied that it is possible and practicable to do so in the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the court is satisfied that the interests of justice so require and that it is possible and practicable to do so in the circumstances" [may-where]

-- src:10897 | Definition of photograph
-- src:10898 | (8) In this section, photograph includes a still photograph, a photographic film or plate, a microphotographic film, a photostatic negative, an X-ray film, a motion picture and a videotape.
@ref Criminal Code s 491.2(8) (src:10897-10898)
DECLARE `s 491.2(8) kind of thing` IS ONE OF
    `s 491.2(8) a still photograph`
    `s 491.2(8) a photographic film or plate`
    `s 491.2(8) a microphotographic film`
    `s 491.2(8) a photostatic negative`
    `s 491.2(8) an X-ray film`
    `s 491.2(8) a motion picture`
    `s 491.2(8) a videotape`
    `s 491.2(8) any other kind of thing`

@ref Criminal Code s 491.2(8) (src:10897-10898)
GIVEN thing IS A `s 491.2(8) kind of thing`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 491.2(8) photograph` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `s 491.2(8) a still photograph` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 491.2(8) a photographic film or plate` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 491.2(8) a microphotographic film` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 491.2(8) a photostatic negative` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 491.2(8) an X-ray film` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 491.2(8) a motion picture` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 491.2(8) a videotape` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 491.2(8) any other kind of thing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "In this section, photograph includes"

§ `492 Seizure of explosives`

-- src:10899 | Seizure of explosives
-- src:10900 | 492 (1) Every person who executes a warrant issued under section 487 may seize any explosive substance that they suspect is intended to be used for an unlawful purpose, and shall, as soon as possible, remove to a place of safety anything that they seize under this section and detain it until they are ordered by a judge of a superior court to deliver it to some other person or an order is made under subsection (2).
@ref Criminal Code s 492(1) (src:10899-10900)
GIVEN `the person executes a warrant issued under section 487` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is an explosive substance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person suspects that the thing is intended to be used for an unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492(1) the person may seize the thing` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person executes a warrant issued under section 487` AND `the person suspects that the thing is intended to be used for an unlawful purpose`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person who executes a warrant issued under section 487 may seize any explosive substance that they suspect is intended to be used for an unlawful purpose"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 2 explosive substance: the thing is an explosive substance`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any explosive substance"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "explosive substance" is defined in section 2, answered by the keel

@ref Criminal Code s 492(1) (src:10899-10900)
DECLARE `s 492(1) party` IS ONE OF `s 492(1) the person who executes the warrant`   -- not in the core's Party: NEEDS-CORE.md
DECLARE `s 492(1) action` IS ONE OF `s 492(1) remove to a place of safety anything that they seize under this section and detain it`

@ref Criminal Code s 492(1) (src:10899-10900)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 492(1) party` `s 492(1) action`
`s 492(1) the duty of the person who executes the warrant to remove and detain what they seize` MEANS
    PARTY `s 492(1) the person who executes the warrant`
    MUST `s 492(1) remove to a place of safety anything that they seize under this section and detain it`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 492(1) the person who executes the warrant` BECAUSE "what the person seized was not removed to a place of safety and detained"

@ref Criminal Code s 492(1) (src:10899-10900)
GIVEN `the thing was seized under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a judge of a superior court has ordered the person to deliver it to some other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 492(1) the thing shall be detained` MEANS
    IF NOT `the thing was seized under this section`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is for "anything that they seize under this section"
    ELSE IF `a judge of a superior court has ordered the person to deliver it to some other person` OR `an order is made under subsection (2)`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "detain it until they are ordered by a judge of a superior court to deliver it to some other person or an order is made under subsection (2)"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

